<title>AUSTRALIA: Wiluna WNA half yr profit A$2 mln after sale.</title>
<headline>Wiluna WNA half yr profit A$2 mln after sale.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    0.05  vs  1.38</p>
<p>    Net				     1.99  vs  loss 0.55</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cents)	  nil   vs  nil</p>
<p>    Sales				  32.85  vs 28.89</p>
<p>    Other income			  0.28  vs  1.16</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   1.23  vs  loss 0.53</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	     profit 1.95  vs  loss 2.23</p>
<p>    Tax				     0.01  vs  credit 0.31</p>
<p>    Interest				0.20  vs  0.31</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  6.53  vs  5.04</p>
<p>    Minorities			    nil   vs  nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Wiluna Mines Ltd is a Western Australian gold miner. The company said the half-year result includes an abnormal gain arising from the sale of its Miranda tenements of A$4.2 million, offset by provisions against listed investments and exploration interests totalling A$2.2 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
